first_light.desc.light_colour=Makes block light more saturated, so glowstone, lava and lanterns tint the walls. 0 keeps their colours.
first_light.desc.light_strength=How bright block lights, their glow and held lights are. Higher lights dark rooms more.
first_light.desc.god_rays=Haze in the air that shows sun shafts through windows and leaves. Higher is thicker. Needs Volumetric Light, and Bedrock Volumetric Fog off (the pack's default).
first_light.desc.dusk_fog=How much thicker the haze gets at sunrise and sunset. 0 keeps it the same all day.
first_light.desc.sky_blue=A deeper, more saturated blue where you look at the sky. Its light on the world stays Radiante's.
first_light.desc.polish=Makes already smooth surfaces glossier. Rough ones stay as they are. 0 turns it off.
first_light.desc.water_mirror=Calmer, smoother water with sharper reflections. 0 keeps Radiante's waves.
first_light.desc.bloom=Glow round the sun, lamps and bright windows. Higher is a bigger glow.
first_light.desc.contrast=Darker shadows and brighter highlights. 0 turns it off.
first_light.desc.saturation=Colour strength of the finished picture. 1 keeps it.

first_light.preset.first_light=First Light
first_light.preset.first_light.desc=The 2020 Xbox Series X DXR demo: clear god rays, a deep blue sky, vivid lights and punchy contrast.
first_light.preset.gamescom=Gamescom 2019
first_light.preset.gamescom.desc=The 2019 reveal: thick fog and shafts, stronger colour, brighter block light and more bloom.
first_light.preset.softer=Softer
first_light.preset.softer.desc=The same look toned down: light haze, gentler contrast and colour.
